description: "\"pillars[10]: Correctness,Reliability,Maintainability,Scalability,Security,Performance,Simplicity,Observability,Testability,Evolvability design[17]: Understand Problem,→,Identify Constraints,→,Explore Alternatives,→,Evaluate Tradeoffs,→,Select Architecture,→,Implement,→,Validate,→,Operate,→,Improve decision[13]: Understand,→,Analyze,→,Predict,→,Compare,→,Decide,→,Measure,→,Reflect constraints[13]: Time,Budget,Memory,CPU,Storage,Network,Reliability,Latency,Throughput,Team Size,Skill Level,Regulations,Business Goals tradeoffs[18]: Performance,↔,Maintainability,Simplicity,↔,Flexibility,Consistency,↔,Availability,Latency,↔,Cost,Speed,↔,Quality,Security,↔,Convenience mindset[8]: Think In Systems,Think In Constraints,Think In Tradeoffs,Think In Failure Modes,Think In Lifecycles,Think In Evidence,Think In Feedback Loops,Think Long Term failures[5]: Failures Are Normal,Failures Reveal Assumptions,Every Failure Produces Knowledge,Every Failure Should Improve The System,Root Cause Matters More Than Symptoms quality[9]: Useful,Correct,Understandable,Testable,Observable,Maintainable,Extensible,Reliable,Secure anti_patterns[10]: Premature Optimization,Cargo Cult Programming,Over Engineering,Under Engineering,Copy Without Understanding,Hidden Complexity,Magic Numbers,Tight Coupling,Unnecessary Abstraction,Untested Assumptions every_decision_requires[10]: Objective,Context,Constraints,Alternatives,Tradeoffs,Risks,Assumptions,Evidence,Expected Outcome,Validation lifecycle[19]: Discover,→,Understand,→,Design,→,Build,→,Test,→,Deploy,→,Operate,→,Observe,→,Improve,→,Retire success[6]: Solves Real Problems,Meets Constraints,Survives Change,Minimizes Complexity,Produces Reusable Knowledge,Improves Future Decisions guarantees[7]: Every generated company follows engineering laws.,Every repository evolves realistically.,Every architecture contains explicit tradeoffs.,Every bug has an explainable cause.,Every optimization has measurable justification.,Every lesson becomes reusable knowledge.,Every Engineering Knowledge Record preserves engineering reasoning.\""
spec:
  id: engineering_principles
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: critical
  module: Core
  compiler_stage: Foundation
  description: "\"\\\"Defines the universal engineering principles that govern every Engineering Knowledge Record (EKR), engineering world, company, repository, architecture, artifact, and engineering decision generated by the TOON Dataset Compiler. These principles are technology-independent and represent timeless engineering knowledge.\\\"\""
purpose: "\"\\\"Define immutable engineering principles that every generated engineering artifact must satisfy regardless of programming language, framework, platform, or domain.\\\"\""
engineering:
  definition: "\"\\\"Engineering is the disciplined process of designing, building, validating, operating, maintaining and evolving systems under constraints to satisfy real-world objectives.\\\"\""
laws:
  L01:
    name: Every System Exists For A Purpose
    explanation: No component should exist without solving a meaningful problem.
  L02:
    name: Every Decision Has Context
    explanation: Engineering decisions cannot be evaluated without understanding surrounding constraints.
  L03:
    name: Every Design Has Tradeoffs
    explanation: There are no universally optimal solutions.
  L04:
    name: Every Optimization Has Cost
    explanation: Improvements in one dimension usually reduce performance in another.
  L05:
    name: Every Abstraction Leaks
    explanation: Abstractions simplify systems but never completely hide implementation details.
  L06:
    name: Complexity Grows Naturally
    explanation: Complexity increases unless actively managed.
  L07:
    name: Technical Debt Compounds
    explanation: Poor engineering decisions accumulate long-term costs.
  L08:
    name: Reliability Requires Redundancy
    explanation: Critical systems should tolerate failures.
  L09:
    name: Measurement Precedes Optimization
    explanation: Never optimize without evidence.
  L10:
    name: Correctness Before Performance
    explanation: Fast incorrect systems remain incorrect.
  L11:
    name: Simplicity Scales Better
    explanation: "\"\\\"Simpler systems are easier to evolve, debug and maintain.\\\"\""
  L12:
    name: Knowledge Is Reusable
    explanation: Lessons learned should improve future systems.
future:
  language_independent: true
  framework_independent: true
  platform_independent: true
  timeless: true
  reusable: true
  universal: true
